# L §4.6 Readings: "With no reading on or before d, last and since are holes (HOLE-NOREADING)"; L §8.1 HOLE-NOREADING
# "<x>[k] has no reading on or before <d>". r's one reading is at 2026-06-01. q3: "since(x[k], d) is the age in days of
# the last reading": 2026-06-11 - 2026-06-01 = 10. (Was REFCORE-UNSPECIFIED §4.6, the holes of last and since.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
input r: num reading

version v
  cite s
  known 2026-01-01
  r = 5 at 2026-06-01 "s"

ask q1: last(r, 2026-03-01) law 2026-12-31
ask q2: since(r, 2026-03-01) law 2026-12-31
ask q3: since(r, 2026-06-11) law 2026-12-31
=== expect
q1: ?"r has no reading on or before 2026-03-01" (r)
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-12-31
q2: ?"r has no reading on or before 2026-03-01" (r)
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-12-31
q3: 10
  law date 2026-12-31, cut 2026-12-31
